      "side": 1,
      "message": "At that time, I helped Vinayak to help to resolve the issue but yeah, it was reverted by some benchmark, unfortunately.\n\nThe reason I supported Vinayak\u0027s patch at that time was it could cause *regression* for some workload via changing the access bit artificially and it also could affect vmpressure logic.  \n\nHowever, upstream decided taking a risk of the regression and improved a lot since then.\nAndroid also start to rely on PSI rather than vmpressure.\n\nFurthermore, such kinds of access bit stuff is just heuristic so some workload even could get a benefit for the change while some workload are not. IOW, we couldn\u0027t say it\u0027s universally good/bad for every workload. What we \n\nBased on the such thinking, I\u0027d like to follow upstream way rather than taking another fragmentation of MM between upstream and android kernel.",
